# Project One Move-Between-Rooms Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: conceptual support for M6; movement design for M7
#
# Review the course-provided movement flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, WHILE, SET, or similar terms.

SET current_room
SET room_item
SET inventory
SET available_directions

OUTPUT "You are currently in " + current_room
OUTPUT "Which direction would you like to move?"
OUTPUT "Enter North, South, East, West."
INPUT direction

IF room_item is not none AND room_item is not in inventory
    OUTPUT "You must collect the " + room_item + " before leaving this room."

ELSE IF direction is in available_directions

SET current_room to the room connected in the requested direction
OUTPUT "You moved " + direction + "."
OUTPUT "You are now in " + current_room

ELSE
    OUTPUT "You cannot move " + direction + " from" + current_room + "."

END IF

WHILE game is not over
    RETURN TO GAME LOOP
END WHILE
